# Keeps the docker-compose build context small - source is bind-mounted at
# runtime anyway (see docker-compose.yml), so none of this ever needs to
# reach the Docker daemon at build time. Mirrors the various .gitignore
# files' build-artifact entries.
#
# build-linux/build_release-linux (Dockerfile.linux-ci's and
# Dockerfile.linux-release's own build directory names, used specifically
# so they don't collide with macOS-native build/build_release on a
# bind-mounted checkout) matter here too, and for a stronger reason than
# the plain build/build_release entries below: Dockerfile.linux-release
# actually COPYs the build context in (Dockerfile.linux-ci only bind-
# mounts, never COPYs) - a stale backend/build-linux/CMakeCache.txt left
# on the host by an earlier `docker compose run backend` (Ubuntu-based,
# CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=/usr/bin/c++) getting copied into a fresh Rocky-8-
# based release build fails immediately (that compiler path doesn't exist
# there) - confirmed by hitting exactly this failure before adding this
# entry.
.git
**/build
**/build_release
**/build-linux
**/build_release-linux
**/.dart_tool
**/.pub-cache
**/generated
**/generated_tcl
**/__pycache__
backend/src/lefdef/**/lib
backend/src/lefdef/**/include
backend/src/lefdef/**/bin
# lef_lib's own BUILD_IN_SOURCE Makefile scatters these directly into
# src/lefdef/lef's subdirectories (backend/.gitignore has the same
# entries) - a stale one left on the host by an earlier native/Docker
# build (e.g. an arm64 Linux .o from a Docker run on this Apple Silicon
# Mac) getting copied into a fresh x86_64 release container fails the
# link with a "wrong format"/relocation error - confirmed by hitting
# exactly this failure before adding these entries.
backend/src/lefdef/**/*.o
backend/src/lefdef/**/*.a
backend/src/lefdef/**/lef.tab.cpp
backend/src/lefdef/**/lef.tab.h
backend/src/lefdef/**/lef.output
frontend/.flutter-plugins-dependencies
flutter_plugin/.flutter-plugins-dependencies
